window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>A story of desire, control, and transformation.</b></p> <p>Geraldine Collins is shy, soft spoken, and nearly invisible in the retail job she’s held for years. But behind the oversized sweaters and downcast eyes lies a storm of unspoken hunger. She’s tired of being the woman who says nothing, wants everything, and never dares to ask.</p> <p>Everything changes when she discovers a mysterious BDSM party and a silver mask that awakens the powerful, commanding version of herself she never knew existed. As Scarlet, she becomes a dominant force. Desired, feared, and adored. But the line between fantasy and identity begins to blur.</p> <p>With the guidance of a seductive coworker, a dominant mentor, and a circle of beautifully broken souls, Geraldine learns that being a freak isn’t something to hide. It is something to honor.</p> <p>Raw, erotic, and emotionally charged, <i>What She Does in the Dark</i> is a story of liberation, sexual awakening, and what happens when a woman finally says yes to herself.</p>"; 
